From f8f4bdc951c6f9b6d1a9fcdb4003921f21ce98a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haitham Ahmed <haitham2020ahmed@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MAP: add a one-time server-side bulk importer for NWEA PDFs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds /admin/bulk-map-import, a one-time admin tool that runs every PDF
sitting in assets/pending-map-imports/ through the exact same import
pipeline the normal MAP upload page uses (importMapFile) — same
parsing, same duplicate/ambiguous-name handling, same MAP plans.

Built because this round's assistant (working the live site through a
remote browser, no push access) had no way to drive the site's native
"Choose File" dialog — a real OS window, not part of the page — since
the Claude-in-Chrome extension was offline this session. This gives a
server-side door into the same import pipeline that needs no browser
file-picker at all: drop PDFs in the repo, push, click one button.

Includes this round's 8 NWEA files for grades 4A/4B/6A (2 ASG, 6 Class
Profile). Each file is deleted right after a successful import so this
page (or a redeploy) can never import the same file twice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015fkTM92JrqCiox9RNegECN
